## 2. Sculpting: ZBrush for Character and Creature Art

Digital sculpting forms the foundation of modern character production. **Naughty Dog, Santa Monica Studio, and Guerrilla Games** have shared extensive GDC documentation on their character pipelines, making this domain particularly well-documented.

### Top-tier courses and the industry hierarchy

**Gnomon Workshop** ($49/month or $490/year) represents the highest tier. **Madeleine Scott-Spencer’s “Introduction to ZBrush 2024”** consistently ranks as Gnomon’s most popular course. Scott-Spencer worked at Weta Workshop/Digital on The Hobbit trilogy, Pacific Rim 2, and The Witcher, and authored the definitive ZBrush Character Creation, ZBrush Creature Design, and ZBrush Digital Sculpting: Human Anatomy books. Her courses provide 19+ hours of instruction with direct film/game production relevance.

**Ryan Kingslien** occupies legendary status—he joined the original ZBrush team, created the Rake brush, and has trained over **25,000 artists at ILM, Blizzard, and EA Shanghai**. His “Anatomy For Artists” course and “Digital Sculpting Method” define how professionals approach figure construction. His emphasis on seeing the body as a unified whole rather than collected parts transforms how students understand form.

**FlippedNormals**, founded by VFX veterans with credits on Pacific Rim Uprising and Alien Covenant, offers practical game-focused content. Their **“Creating a Full Character in ZBrush”** (18-hour Souls-inspired character) and “Hard Surface Character Sculpting” by Richie Jon Mason (former Guerrilla Games) specifically target game production.

**Michael Pavlovich** (Lead Character Artist at Certain Affinity, credits on Halo 4, Halo MCC, Call of Duty, Doom) provides a **12-part “Intro to ZBrush” series** with portions available free. His “ZBrush for Ideation” contains 300+ videos. Regular ZBrushLIVE streams offer free ongoing education.

**Follygon** runs the annual Sculptober challenge and emphasizes repeatable workflows. “ZBrush 101: ZBrush for Absolute Beginners” and “Sculpting The Planes of the Head” (20 stages) build foundational confidence.

### GDC talks on character production pipelines

**“Character Technology of The Last of Us Part II”** (GDC 2021) details Naughty Dog’s character tools evolution, shaders, and gore systems. Lead artists Frank Tzeng (Joel, Abby) and Soa Lee (Ellie) managed the studio’s largest character production, using practical blood/gore simulation shoots for authenticity.

Santa Monica Studio’s **“Animation in God of War: Ragnarok”** (GDC 2023) by Bruno Velazquez covers joint-based rigging for volume preservation and dynamic bone technique for muscle/fat/skin jiggle. **“Reinventing God of War”** (GDC 2019) explains the complete character philosophy reimagining.

Guerrilla Games’ **“Repopulating the Earth: Character Production on Horizon Zero Dawn”** (GDC 2018) and **“Creating the Many Faces of Horizon Forbidden West”** (GDC 2022) demonstrate massive outsourcing pipeline management with small internal teams and detailed external briefs.

### Japanese sculptors and resources

**Takayuki Takeya (竹谷隆之)**, born 1963, represents Japan’s premier creature designer with credits on Shin-Godzilla’s evolutionary stages, Attack on Titan, and the legendary Giant God Warrior. His art books “畏怖の造形” (Sculptures Collection) and “Drawings Arrangement and Design” document his approach to detail and traditional motif integration.

**Yuuji Katagiri (片桐裕司)** bridges Japanese and Western production with Hollywood credits on Pacific Rim and Man of Steel. His book **“片桐裕司のアナトミー・スカルプティング 完全版”** (Anatomy Sculpting Complete Edition) teaches his hybrid techniques.

**Visutor** (visutor.com) offers Japanese ZBrush courses taught by Disney alumni. **3DTotal Japan** provides the “ZBrush の基本を知る” series. **Pixologic Japan YouTube** hosts official Japanese tutorials. Japanese figure culture—particularly Max Factory’s workflows and Wonder Festival showcase culture—influences character production aesthetics.

Japanese books include **“作って覚える！ZBrushフィギュア制作チュートリアル”** by ウチヤマ リュウタ (ZBrush 2022) covering figure creation through painting, and the Japanese edition of “Anatomy For Sculptors.”

### Chinese resources

**琅泽中文CG教程 (阿彪时间)** on Bilibili provides a comprehensive **ZBrush 4R7 tutorial series (120+ videos)**. **Aniraiden** covers ZBrush iPad workflows and figure creation. **专注于游戏建模** focuses on game modeling including Honor of Kings characters.

The **火熊网 (Huoxiong)** community serves as a major Chinese 2D/3D art hub. **ZBrush中文网站** (zbrush.mairuan.com) aggregates Chinese tutorials and resources.

### The essential anatomy book

**“Anatomy for Sculptors: Understanding the Human Figure”** by Uldis Zarins and Sandis Kondrats is the **industry gold standard**—used by Fortiche Production’s character team on Arcane Season 1. The visual-first approach (2% text) pairs 3D models with live model photos featuring muscle overlays and clear topology diagrams. This Kickstarter-funded book revolutionized how artists learn anatomy for digital production. The companion “Anatomy of Facial Expressions” extends the methodology to faces.

**“ZBrush Digital Sculpting: Human Anatomy”** by Scott Spencer (Weta Workshop, credits on Iron Man, Golden Axe) provides a complete sculpting tutorial from skeleton to muscle to skin with video instruction and anatomy models included.

